+-----------------------------------------------------------------------
| Running ${PKGSTEM} on OpenBSD
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------

This package links the base-system LibreSSL rather than
security/openssl. Node selects its legacy ncrypto backend because
LibreSSL reports OPENSSL_VERSION_NUMBER 0x20000000L and does not define
OPENSSL_VERSION_MAJOR. Do not treat process.versions.openssl as an
OpenSSL 3 release.

The following upstream features are unavailable and fail closed:
--secure-heap, pskCallback, asynchronous certificate and OCSPRequest
callbacks, scrypt, XOF digests, Ed448, X448, SM2, OCB and multi-prime
RSA. Raw TLS ticket bytes, getSharedSigalgs and asynchronous
certificate callbacks are rejected instead of silently ignored.

LibreSSL does not provide the client-hello and per-connection
certificate-store interfaces used by recent upstream TLS hardening.
The SNI pinning and session-binding paths added for CVE-2026-123872 and
the certificate-store mitigation for CVE-2026-123867 are therefore not
compiled in this build. Server-side SNI and session configurations need
a native security review before they are exposed to untrusted clients.
The port's LibreSSL re-read path also calls ClearOut() from DoWrite();
nested-write re-entry needs native review against the new cycle guard.

Compilation, generated package contents, V8, TLS, pledge/unveil and the
complete regression suite still require validation on a native OpenBSD
host. Static patch review is not runtime evidence.
